DESCRIPTION:(1246) Chaka hides a magnitude 11.8 star\, seen from Kota.\nThe
  predicted edge passes 5 km to the NW\, so a miss is likely — but a chor
 d from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClosest app
 roach 00:45:19 IST\, give or take 2 s. The star is 21° up in the NE · da
 rk sky.\nIt fades 3.3 magnitudes for up to 1.1 s on the centre line\, and 
 the path is 18 km wide\, give or take 13 km.\nThe map\, the finder chart a
 nd the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroid?e=2026-09-12-1246-ch
