SUMMARY:(1633) Chimay hides a mag 11.5 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(1633) Chimay hides a magnitude 11.5 star\, seen from Kota.\nTh
 e predicted edge passes 4 km to the SSE\, so a miss is likely — but a ch
 ord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClosest a
 pproach 23:45:27 IST\, give or take 1 s. The star is 51° up in the SSE ·
  dark sky.\nIt fades 4.1 magnitudes for up to 2.6 s on the centre line\, a
 nd the path is 37 km wide\, give or take 36 km.\nThe map\, the finder char
 t and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroid?e=2027-08-29-1633
 -chimay-339904
